# Core texts enter through two doors

The legal door asks whether an exact edition can be copied and transformed.
The relational door asks whether its people or steward authorize this use.
Neither answer may overwrite the other.

A public webpage is not an open corpus.
A public-domain edition is not community consent, and a public-domain finding
in one jurisdiction is not automatically a worldwide finding.
An open license is not permission to ignore an explicit cultural protocol.
Old is not ownerless.

The first movement therefore admits source identity before source body:

    metadata -> rights witness + jurisdiction/scope
             -> community/steward protocol
             -> exact edition/item -> fresh admission -> segment

The acknowledgement is always one of:

    nothing  unresolved rights, item, or authority
    0        explicit refusal or incompatible restriction
    1        admitted exact segment at the witnessed epoch
    node     a concrete review/re-witness route

The 36-layer spine is:

    01 source identity          19 identity role
    02 legal rights             20 inclusion / boundary
    03 community authority      21 relationship
    04 cultural restriction     22 place
    05 provenance               23 time
    06 work                     24 action
    07 edition                  25 state
    08 segment                  26 feeling
    09 age                      27 modality
    10 language                 28 negation
    11 dialect                  29 composition
    12 script                   30 causality
    13 transliteration          31 evidence
    14 morphology               32 uncertainty
    15 syntax                   33 metaphor
    16 speaker                  34 translation alignment / loss
    17 addressee                35 query
    18 viewpoint               36 response / receipt / freshness

This is a versioned scaffold, not an assertion that every language or
knowledge system divides reality into these categories. A community may add a
different projection without changing the layer symbols or the source text.

Each layer has a compact local symbol 1..36. Each layer/lane pair has a compact
query symbol 1..252 over WHAT, WHERE, WHEN, WHO, HOW, WHICH, WHY. A completed
derived node may become the next query subject. The executable 36-layer walk
uses two explicit 18-step waves: the inherited base-8 derivation path lives in
a signed integer and cannot honestly hold one 36-deep path. The checkpoint is
visible structure, not a silent reset. Surface language remains evidence
attached to the node, never the node's identity.

Translation alignment is not equivalence. Four public-domain surfaces of
Genesis 1:1 share one proposed alignment group in the seed, while retaining
four source identities, four edition receipts, and four surface strings.
Loss, disagreement, and translator choice belong at layer 34; they must not be
collapsed away in pursuit of a single "core" sentence.

For Indigenous and traditional knowledge, absence of a restriction is not
proof of permission. Community-created Local Contexts labels, where present,
outrank a generic institutional guess. Culturally sensitive, secret/sacred,
seasonal, gender-restricted, community-only, and non-commercial protocols stay
machine-visible. The kernel may offer a relationship node; it may not mint
consent on a community's behalf.

The first six edition-bound seed segments are intentionally small. Project
Gutenberg's public-domain findings are recorded as U.S.-scoped, with a
jurisdiction recheck owed before downstream redistribution elsewhere. Web
footnote markers are excluded and line breaks are normalized to spaces; each
locator and edition URI remains attached. They prove the intake path, not
corpus breadth. Popol Vuh metadata enters while its colonial English
mediation waits for K'iche' community guidance. AILLA waits for an exact
collection/item. FirstVoices' no-scrape/no-merge terms are honored as 0.
SuttaCentral's request against AI-dataset use is honored as 0 despite CC0.
African Storybook waits for an exact story license. StoryWeaver offers a node
until an exact book and its creator/translator attribution are selected.

North star: invite living communities to choose the texts, labels, benefits,
and questions. The kernel's first Indigenous sentence should arrive through a
relationship, not an extraction.

The first relationship door is now executable:
`learn/hati-suci-core-text-invitation.fk` records Hati Suci as pilot 1 through
an initiating member. Satsang selected Giles' "The Light Hubs" first; source
13 records its exact supplied hash and the member-witnessed scoped author
permission as metadata-only. That moves it from unresolved to a review node.
The initiating member records no additional sacred or community-use
restrictions; the row remains a review node because it is metadata-only. The
initiating member also records no additional benefit/reciprocity condition.
Freshness is recorded as no scheduled review with re-witness on change. All
nine terms are now complete; the next action asks Satsang for final
ratification. The initiating member now reports that ratification, opening the
source protocol. The row remains a review node because the body is
metadata-only. The next action selects a revocable carrier or explicitly
withholds the complete surface.

This spine composes with the body's existing core-word acknowledgement and
core-word inquiry. Those organs own lower/UPPER clusivity and the five natural
inquiry words; this cell adds the 36 source/meaning/receipt coordinates and the
seven-plane address walk (including WHO and WHICH) without redefining them.
